 degree but want  to move into a technical field  um what would you advise them about  how to position themselves to employers  what things emphasize  in making that particular kind of  transition  so like i said any transition is like  a plane taking off right it's not going  to be easy  it's it'll take a lot of efforts you  know to gain the thrust  it takes a lot of efforts right and even  to go down it takes a lot of efforts  right cruising is the best time so when  you're transitioning  it is more like the trust that you need  to gain which means  that in a normal scenario if you were  doing five things  in a transition phase you have to do 15  things just because you  are transitioning and that effort means  that  you will look at projects you will look  for internships you can look at learning  opportunities  your focus has to be that i want to do  this work  and not can i make this much money out  of it right you cannot sail on both  boats so you have to have to have  maximized efforts  when you're transitioning people will  not believe you in general people  do not like to believe anybody's  transition oh you must be  a fool to actually leave such a good  career and move there  i mean they want to understand that  there is a reason why you are deciding  to transition  so you don't need to have to explain to  them but keep  you know maximizing your efforts very  critical to find  projects internship free work  opportunities where you get to learn  because that learning will get you a job  very good  um by the way in general  i'm going to assume that everything you  have said applies not just for tech jobs  but for  anybody who's looking for any job yes  absolutely absolutely and there's  nothing that i've told that people don't  know  i think all of us know this it's just  that they're organizing their wardrobe  so they'll be able to pick up the right  set of  you know clothes when they have to go  out  uh ishmael and our linkedin audience i  think this may be our  last question due to time um  how would you get through to a specific  company  if you want to apply for a job  how would you um so  he's expressing some frustration about  applying through job boards  and web portals  when looking to get to a particular  company  so what would the strategy be if you  said for example i want to work  for um  therapy and  how do you get to a company in  particular  you know i think uh sometimes we beat  ourselves  up for no fault of ours because somebody  is not responding  somebody is not engaging it's not your  fault and a lot of times people  get very disillusioned in the job search  process when  you know they don't get responses they  get very rejected saying that  oh i have applied to 50 jobs nobody is  responding to me don't don't do that to  you because it's not on you  it's on people who have not possibly  responded to you but what i would do  like i said when i was in a job search  stage  every day morning i would wake up smell  the coffee  apply to 10 relevant jobs if out of  those 10 there are two places that i  really want to work in  i will go to linkedin look up for two or  three relevant people  try to write an email to them saying  that hey apply to this job could you  refer me  could you help me etc etc i would also  try to talk in my network if anybody  knows anybody in that company  to see if somebody can put a word  through  basically what i'm saying is i'm trying  in different  aspects and angles to get through people  because i want that  and even after that if you don't land  that opportunity  don't worry it's not that you will never  land that opportunity  but what is important is to not beat  yourself up because  when you beat yourself up you become low  on confidence when you become low on  confidence you're not  able to be your best at interview  conversations  and you don't want to be not at your  best when  when you go for any interview because  it's a job  after all that you get  what wonderful a